messages:
maria-support: Hey team — escalating a customer-repro. They see a spike of 504s and `context canceled` in logs when p95 latency crosses ~200ms. They're on Go SDK v0.9.1, using a custom http.Client constructed per request. Attached minimal repro and logs.

kyle-eng: Can you paste the client/transport code and the retry settings you pass to the SDK? Also show the exact error traces.

maria-support: Sure — minimal snippet from customer:
```go
func do(ctx context.Context, req *http.Request) (*http.Response, error) {
    client := &http.Client{
        Transport: &http.Transport{
            DisableKeepAlives: false,
        },
    }
    req = req.WithContext(ctx)
    return client.Do(req)
}
// SDK configured with retries: maxAttempts=3, baseBackoff=100ms, retryOn=5xx,io_err
// They call with ctx that has 300ms deadline.
```
Logs: `context canceled` during second attempt, backend returns 504 on a few requests.

kyle-eng: Two quick problems visible: 1) creating a new *http.Client* / Transport per request kills connection reuse — TLS+DNS handshake overhead increases latency and can push you over the deadline. 2) mixing per-request context deadlines with SDK-level retry loop means the same ctx gets reused across attempts and may be expired on retries, producing `context canceled` instead of a clean retry.

kyle-eng: Repro tips: reuse a single client/transport across requests, or set a per-attempt context inside the SDK retry loop. Example change:
```go
var sharedTransport = &http.Transport{
    MaxIdleConns: 100,
    MaxIdleConnsPerHost: 100,
    IdleConnTimeout: 90 * time.Second,
    TLSHandshakeTimeout: 10 * time.Second,
}
var sharedClient = &http.Client{Transport: sharedTransport}
// In request path: // ctx is request-scoped outer ctx
attemptCtx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, attemptTimeout)
defer cancel()
req = req.WithContext(attemptCtx)
resp, err := sharedClient.Do(req)
```

jordan-sre: Also check socket exhaustion — if they spin up lots of short-lived transports, the server or client can hit ephemeral port exhaustion or thread pool pressure. Recommend increasing `MaxIdleConnsPerHost` and `MaxIdleConns`, and set `ResponseHeaderTimeout` and `IdleConnTimeout`. If library code recreates transport on each retry, it leaks sockets.

jordan-sre: We had a similar support case — observed `504` + `context canceled` when client.Timeout==0 (no client-level timeout) and ctx had short deadline; idle connections were not reused so median p90 jumped.

sam-ml: Quick workaround if customer can't change app immediately: configure the SDK to not reuse the outer ctx for retries. In v0.10.x we added a flag `retry_on_context_cancel` (default changed) and internal behavior to create per-attempt contexts. If they upgrade to v0.10.2 it should behave better. Alternatively, set SDK retry policy to apply per-attempt time budget.

sam-ml: Example: wrap the SDK call like
```go
// give each attempt 250ms, keep outer ctx for cancellation only
perAttempt := func() (*Response, error) {
    attemptCtx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 250*time.Millisecond)
    defer cancel()
    req = req.WithContext(attemptCtx)
    return client.Do(req)
}
```

maria-support: Good pointers — customer can't upgrade today. They can reuse a shared client though. I'll send a patch to do that and adjust MaxIdleConns. If that reduces 504s we can close.

kyle-eng: Also add `client.Timeout` only if you want a hard deadline independent of ctx. Beware `client.Timeout` cancels the request by canceling the request context under the hood. Prefer per-attempt context in retry loops so you don't exhaust the allowed attempts.

maria-support: One more log snippet they provided: `retry loop attempt 2: context canceled` followed by `http status 504`. Looks like attempt 1 was slow, consumed outer ctx, attempt 2 ran but ctx already expired.

jordan-sre: TL;DR action items: 1) Ask customer to reuse http.Client/Transport across requests. 2) Set MaxIdleConnsPerHost to >100 for bursty clients. 3) Configure per-attempt timeouts inside retry loop. 4) Suggest upgrading SDK to v0.10.2 where retry/context behavior is improved.

maria-support: I'll provision a quick patch and test with them tomorrow. Thanks @kyle-eng @jordan-sre @sam-ml :thumbsup:

